<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH SPT 9MO GROSS DOWN-CZECH ACCOUNTING.</title>
<headline>CZECH SPT 9MO GROSS DOWN-CZECH ACCOUNTING.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for nine</p>
<p>months ending September 30, 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross profit		  6,307.237  vs	6,862.677</p>
<p> Operating profit	    6,534.666  vs	6,972.178</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services		 20,833.679  vs     17,108.132</p>
<p> Sales of goods		  354.240  vs	  953.992</p>
<p> Production		   21,832.969  vs     17,512.834</p>
<p> Depreciation		  3,502.884  vs	2,188.776</p>
<p> Total assets		 98,830.550  vs     96,287.921</p>
<p> Basic capital		32,208.990  vs     32,208.990</p>
<p>Note. Full name of the monopoly Czech fixed-line phone</p>
<p>operator is SPT Telecom a.s. . Results, calculated</p>
<p>under Czech accounting standards, were provided by the Prague</p>
<p>Stock Exchange (PSE). Results prepared under international</p>
<p>accounting standards were released last week. Dutch-Swiss</p>
<p>consortium Telsource of Koninklijke PTT Nederland NV </p>
<p>and Swiss Telecom holds 27 percent of SPT. SPT is listed on</p>
<p>the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
